## 6. Icon System

### Icon Package Structure

```
packages/icons/src/
├── svgs/              # 2598 SVG source files
├── fonts/
│   ├── native/CoinbaseIcons.ttf
│   └── web/CoinbaseIcons-*.woff2
├── glyphMap.ts        # Icon name → glyph mapping
├── IconName.ts        # Type definitions
└── names.ts           # Icon name list
```

### Icon Sizes

| Size | Pixels | Usage |
|------|--------|-------|
| `xs` | 12px | Tight spaces, inline with small text |
| `s` | 16px | Compact buttons, small controls |
| `m` | 24px | Default, most common |
| `l` | 32px | Large buttons, emphasis |

### Icon Usage

```tsx
// Web
import { Icon } from '@coinbase/cds-web/icons/Icon';
<Icon name="arrow-right" size="m" color="fgPrimary" />

// Mobile
import { Icon } from '@coinbase/cds-mobile/icons/Icon';
<Icon name="arrow-right" size="m" color="fgPrimary" />
```

### Icon Naming Convention

Icons follow the pattern: `{name}-{size}-{state}`

- Names use kebab-case: `arrow-right`, `chevron-down`, `wallet-outlined`
- States: `active` (filled) or `inactive` (outlined)

